{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/939828-using-backgrounds-from-m20-in-games-of-demon-the-fallen","id":939828,"title":"Using Backgrounds from M20 in games of Demon: The Fallen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-29T15:30:57-07:00","id":939828,"title":"Using Backgrounds from M20 in games of Demon: The Fallen","content":"Mage 20 has more Backgrounds than I've seen in any other WoD game. Some of them I feel can really add to other WoD games. In my example, Demon. Going over the list I've managed to divide the Backgrounds into four groups: the ones already in Demon, the ones that can be added easy enough, the ones that need some work and the ones that cannot, either because they're intricately linked with Mage or are already represented with a very similiar Background.<br /> <br /> <b>Already in Demon:</b><br /> Allies<br /> Contacts<br /> Eminence<br /> Fame<br /> Followers<br /> Influence<br /> Legacy<br /> Mentor<br /> Paragon<br /> Resources<br /> <br /> <b>Can be added:</b><br /> Alternate Identity<br /> Arcane<br /> Backup<br /> Blessing (comes from a holdover from the Demon's time as an Elohim)<br /> Certification<br /> Chantry (standin for an Infernal Court)<br /> Destiny (see Blessing)<br /> Library<br /> Patron<br /> Rank<br /> Spies<br /> Wonder (as per the Enchanted Relics rules in the Demon Players Guide)<br /> <br /> <b>Might be able to be added:</b><br /> Dream (vague memories of the abilities the Demon had as an Elohim)<br /> Legend (living up to the ideal of the Elohim that you once were)<br /> Node (a place that people have Faith in and you can gather it from once per week)<br /> Sanctum (to help in rituals, comes at regular instead of double cost)<br /> <br /> <b>Can't be added:</b><br /> Avatar<br /> Cult (similar function to the Earthbound Cult Background)<br /> Demesne<br /> Enhancement<br /> Familiar<br /> Past Lives (similar function to Legacy)<br /> Requisitions<br /> Retainers (similar function to Followers)<br /> Secret Weapons<br /> Status (similar function to Eminence)<br /> Totem<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not entirely sure on how to work with the ones that might be added. Blessing, Destiny, Dream and Legend especially built around the whole concept of the Elohim life. I'm not entirely sure about the Chantry, Node and Wonder things yet.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? Should I leave a few of them out? Perhaps a few can be done after all? Or is there other overlap I have to keep in mind?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12085,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","user":"Beriorn","date":". 07-31-2016, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T21:20:42-07:00","id":939945,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure rank, spies, Patron and backup are Technocracy only. How would Cult be different than Pacts? And what would Library Do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T02:25:17-07:00","id":940018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/939828-using-backgrounds-from-m20-in-games-of-demon-the-fallen?p=939945#post939945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure rank, spies, Patron and backup are Technocracy only. How would Cult be different than Pacts? And what would Library Do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding those four:<br /> - Backup allows you to call for members of an organisation you are part of to help you out, after which they disperse back to said organisation. The Background (M20 p.306) gives well over a dozen examples of such groups, like hackers, scholars, shamans, spirits, gang members, animals and so on. While not all of them will apply to a Demon, a fair deal of them do.<br /> - Patron is having a mysterious and high-ranking entity take interest in you and help you out, but you are expected to do something in return when asked. This can be a high-ranking and powerful Fallen, or perhaps even an Earthbound.<br /> - Rank is having a title amongst the public, like a military rank, a religious position, a place in a company or a title of nobility. Your duke can actually be a duke.<br /> - Spies is having people in the right places, from the mob and Wall Street all the way up to Infernal Courts and on a worldwide scale, if going above 5 for the latter.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, Cult is more like the Earthbound Background that's called Cult, so this might not be for your regular Fallen.<br /> <br /> Library gives you a collection of information to research certain things. I reckon it's mainly useful for figuring out stuff like bits of True Names.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T10:03:19-07:00","id":940126,"title":"","content":"Why Arcane can't be added?. Mummies (and some vampires) can have it...True Magick isn't mandatory to have it. Some devils might like to act in the shadows, or be mysterious entities known only by those they select. It may represent the highly spiritual nature of Demons hiding them from the eyes of the mundane, or a supernatural skill to not be seen if they don't want to (just like in the old times they hided from the eyes of humans).<br /> <br /> I don't think that Nodes should be ported to Demon...they could diminish the importance of Pacts. Faith it's supposed to come from the direct relationship with humans, putting a place as intermediary doesn't sound good to me. Places with faith (holy land) hurt Tormented Demons, and they should, they're places where humans believe in sacred forces that oppose the workings of evil.<br /> Now, I could see a place that was dedicated to a particular Demon (a black church, if you want), and thus count as blessed land where Tormented Demons can't enter without being hurt...or rather where OTHER Tormented Demons can't enter. Since the faith of the land it's in you, you wouldn't ever suffer it's power. It could also weaken the effect of mortal Unbelief (skeptics watching your lores ain't going to cause an increase on difficulty, because you have more than enough &quot;ambient faith&quot; in your place to pull off whatever you want). So, yes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , I'm not an expert, but I see Sanctums as somewhat more portable to Demon than Nodes.<br /> <br /> Legend seems troublesome to me, like Node, but maybe a bit less if it's used directly in contact with humans. Maybe if you act like a divine/demonic being while using the Revelation, you can reap more faith.<br /> <br /> Blesing, Chantry, Destiny and Wonder can be added without much fuss. Just add them and justify them within the story.<br /> Dream it's a bit wierd, but also easy to port. I, personaly, wouldn't represent it as old knowledge of your times as an Elohim, but rather as an instintive understanding of the true nature of the universe that allows for inmediate knowledge and skill. Dream can be used not only to get skills, but also to get valuable information, like the place where your enemies are hidden, or could hint at the weakness of a powerful enemy. This can't be explained as old knowledge, but can be ported if you say that Demons are so attuned with the Creation that they can get glimpses of it's hidden secrets, if they realy try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T15:20:39-07:00","id":940296,"title":"","content":"The Arcane is coming from the three dot Lore of Humanity power that's a LOT more powerful than Arcane is. Alright, I see where you're coming from with Node. Sanctums have almost all of their benefits affect just Mages, but the bonus on Rituals (from the Demon Players Handbook) can be used. But in this case I'd make Sanctum cost normal instead of double.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T16:32:38-07:00","id":940330,"title":"","content":"I agree about Sanctums should cost normal, but Arcane can't be replaced so easily with the Lore of Humanity. It's not that Arcane it's more powerful, but rather than the two powers do different stuff.<br /> <br /> Lore of Humanity 3 makes you vanish from sight, somewhat like Obfuscate, you have to activate it and can fail, or you may accidentaly cast the Tormented version of the power (which may not be good, dependant on the circumstances).<br /> <br /> Arcane, on the other hand, adds dice to Stealth and substracts dice from Perception or Investigation rolls whenever someone tries to track you down. This advatage applies pasively, frustrating mundane attempts to follow your tracks by evidence that you may have left. For instence, if you buy a gun and then kill someone with that gun, the police might try to track down the weapon, this attempt wouldn't be affected by the Lore of Humanity, but would be affected by Arcane.<br /> Also, it makes information about your character vanish or get lost (which can be bad in a society ruled by information). Rolls made to try to discover any sort of information about your Demon would get very hard. In this way, an Arcane demon would be harder to summon and bind for humans because it will be harder to discover it's Celestial and True Names (as all texts that speak about your Demon tend to get lost), which it's good and bad. It makes life harder to your enemies, but it's also less likely that some random guy would free you from Hell, were you to get send back there. Lore of Humanity 3 doesn't do any of that, it just replaces Stealth.<br /> <br /> Plus, the Background it's cheaper and doesn't need activation. Mages can do everything that Arcane does using Mind/Entropy, but that doesn't really replace the Background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-30-2016, 07:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-31T02:37:27-07:00","id":940548,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, Arcane's in. Updated the list too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}